    "body": "Fixes #297.\n\nHonor `reset_after_epoch=False` by retaining the source state at the end of a limited window. The current implementation resets unconditionally and resets a second time when the flag is enabled.\n\nCheck the offset iterator before advancing the source in `zip`. Otherwise, the loop reads and discards one source sample after reaching the limit, which would also skip a sample when continuation is enabled.\n\nDocument the continuation behavior. Add stateful-source regressions covering empty, short and oversized limits, explicit resets, consecutive windows, checkpoint restoration and uneven per-worker limits.\n\nValidation on macOS CPU with Python 3.12.14 and PyTorch 2.14.1:\n\n- `python -m pytest -q tests/test_dataset.py tests/test_limit_dataset.py`: 34 passed, plus 18 subtests.\n- The limiter regressions expose the unexpected resets and extra reads on unchanged upstream code.\n- Ruff lint, Ruff formatting and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nNo GPU or distributed multi-rank validation was performed.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
